Subject: [PATCH 27/42] loginDialog: Add login options menu to AuthMenuButton
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Now the authMenuButton allows selecting a session type and a login
mechanism.

authPrompt is in charge of:
  * Informing of the available login mechanisms via the "mechanisms-changed"
    signal, it also provides one between them that is selected by default.
  * Getting the selected login mechanism with "selectMechanism" method.

In future commits it will be implemented how UserVerifier emits
"mechanisms-changed".

There are some mechanisms that are not selectable but run in the
background, e.g. fingerprint. These ones won't be at _authMenuButton but
at the new _authIndicatorButton to inform when they are enabled.

Co-authored-by: Marco Trevisan (Treviño) <mail@3v1n0.net>
