From 901bb24c5228ab67f417abfe32c1ffde066be986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Torres Lopez <joantolo@redhat.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 22:25:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 38/42] gdm: Allow starting authServicesLegacy as fallback

There can be cases where authServicesSSSDSwitchable doesn't support some
authentication methods.
In such cases, we should start authServicesLegacy as a fallback for
those unsupported methods.

authServicesSSSDSwitchable leads when the fallback will happen emitting
'mechanisms-changed'. Then unsupportedRoles, from authServicesSSSDSwitchable will
be used to update the enabledRoles in authServicesLegacy.

While authServicesSSSDSwitchable hasn't started its service and didn't receive
